+# Native timed Mid-MPC trajectory admission and guidance
+
+The approved interface change makes the simulator's validated optimized trajectory the authoritative native route. It carries fixed-grid position/course/SOG samples, original issue time, route identity and finite validity. Ordinary operator-route protection remains active.
+
+ARM independently checks initial measured state, source motion limits, sample integration, identity, expiry and immutable renewal. Coordinate transformation preserves points and shares the exact source projection with admission. Guidance preserves timed samples, reads speed by elapsed plan time, retains zero and converts SOG to body surge. Equivalent reanchored local segments retain guidance recovery state. No dynamics, control or allocation source file changed.
+
+The new optional course array uses the implicit ROS empty-array default because Humble's Python generator fails on an explicit [] default. The simulator's native decoder permits omission only for this added array (and explicitly defaulted fields); required historical fields remain strict.
+
+Source manifest SHA256: `8590d52f4b3ee551ae390bb019ffca2a6ad434bd5659a6c92d8f54c870ff9e62`.
+Native library SHA256: `78997104a85bfc5042698d5d9b702058700e342e6e6a0625669719d7ba652277`.
+
+Independent ROS Humble reference: `/home/marine.huang/colav-gnc-oracle/mid-trajectory-20260917-v7`. Thirteen packages compiled from a separately verified/instrumented source tree. The source-only export omits CMake-listed tests, so compilation used BUILD_TESTING=OFF; this is not a ROS unit-suite pass. Ordinary public route-contract callback output parity: coordinate transform 1941 calls/1800 outputs and ARM 1874 calls/20 outputs, no differences. Native tests independently cover the timed admission path.
+
+Standalone contract check:
+
+```sh
+clang++ -std=c++17 -I src/gnc/ship_guidance/include tests/planner_trajectory_contract_test.cpp -o /tmp/gnc-trajectory-contract
+/tmp/gnc-trajectory-contract
+```
+
+The simulator propagates unchanged source limits (0.08 m/s2, 1.2 deg/s, 80 m minimum radius, 0.25 m/s2 lateral acceleration), qualifies the new build, and validates complete ENV ON ownship runs with real IPOPT and no fallback. Final arrival times: OT 858.5 s, HO 781.5 s, crossing give-way 386.5 s, crossing stand-on 409.0 s, exact paper multi-ship 1770.6 s. All end within 308.7 m of the goal and within 10 m of the final mission leg. Full evidence and scope are in Colav-Simulator's `docs/research/2026-09-17-mid-gnc-maneuver-recovery-followup.md` and its `evidence/mid-gnc-trajectory-20260917` directory.
+
+The CS give-way target's legacy terminal overrun/grounding is explicitly deferred by the user. Source control and hydrodynamics were not altered to improve behavior scores or force acceptance.
